Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: restore enumeration after clock context loss

Unicorn RX loses its auto-enumeration table over an idle clock cycle. A
registered WCD938x at device 2 reappears at the enumeration address, while
the old resume path returns success and later reads return stale ID data.
Detect loss of previously attached, bound peripherals before depreparing
clock stop. Reset and re-enumerate using the existing reset-capable path,
waiting for bound peripherals rather than the first enumeration IRQ.
Process reattached peripheral status in a PM-referenced worker after the
manager resume callback completes. Alert handling can synchronously resume
a peripheral, so doing it inside manager resume deadlocks against itself.
Defer IRQ status handling while the manager is resuming as well. Account
for peripherals already reporting ALERT at enumeration, delivering their
initial ATTACHED transition before processing the alert. Only signal
enumeration completion after device zero has gone away and IDs are valid.
Make WCD938x resume wait for initialization after a manager reset before
restoring registers or accepting a new stream. The asynchronous manager
status worker uses no-PM bus operations and can complete this initialization
while the peripheral PM callback is waiting.
Keep runtime PM and the ordinary retained-context clock-stop path enabled.

Compute reset requirements at suspend time, after peripheral properties
are available, instead of overwriting the flag for each enumeration entry.
Propagate clock/resume/deprepare failures and balance clocks on failure.
Reject debugfs accesses when peripheral resume fails or it is unassigned;
ignoring -EACCES on an unbound peripheral can access a clock-gated manager.
A peripheral without a bound/initialized driver has no verified clock-stop
capabilities. Use reset recovery for such a bus instead of interpreting its
zero-initialized properties as support for the extended clock-stop protocol.
On Unicorn, unbound 0217:f001 remains SCP_STAT.CLK_STP_NF=1 after deprepare,
while WCD938x reports ready. This is separate from lost manager context.
Before gating a bus containing unbound peripherals, issue ClockStopNow and
mask bus-clash interrupts. Reset on resume replaces the unsupported extended
prepare/deprepare negotiation; it must not leave an active bus running until
its clock is removed. Keep the pre-existing mode-1-only path unchanged.
For pre-v2 managers, match Qualcomm's reset recovery sequence: reset the
component twice and request a bus reset before restarting frame generation.
Resetting only the manager table leaves peripheral protocol state from the
previous session, with parity faults during re-enumeration. The explicit
bus-reset request is present in the pinned OEM controller implementation.
Do not write legacy bus-reset control on v2 controllers.
No guessed peripheral capabilities or private data are introduced.

